<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!-- THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT. A comment placed ABOVE
         <CustomField> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading "unable to find
         matching parent xml file" error.

         DERIVED, NEVER WRITTEN. This is a FORMULA field, not a stored checkbox — nothing sets
         it directly and it cannot drift out of sync with OwnerId or RecordTypeId the way a
         stamped/stored checkbox maintained by two separate flow writers could.

         BOTH CONDITIONS ARE REQUIRED — DO NOT DROP EITHER ONE.
           1. Owner-is-a-queue: LEFT(CASESAFEID(OwnerId), 3) = "00G" — "00G" is the key prefix
              for a Group/Queue Id, "005" for a User Id. This exact idiom (with "005" for the
              User-owned test) already has in-repo precedent:
              flows/Lead_Intake_Stamp.flow-meta.xml's `fOwnerIsUser` formula resource.
           2. Record type is Investor Onboarding: RecordType.DeveloperName = "Investor_Onboarding".
              🔴 Condition 1 ALONE is NOT sufficient — Acquisition Broker Leads are ALSO
              queue-owned (BrokerPortalService assigns them to a queue), so a formula testing
              only "is the owner a queue" would also read true for Acquisition Broker Leads.
              Both halves together are what scope this to the Investor Onboarding record type's
              own queue-routing workflow.

         RecordType.DeveloperName has in-repo precedent that has passed this org's check-only
         validation (objects/NDA__c/fields/Is_Decline_Allowed__c.field-meta.xml), and Salesforce's
         own "Tips for Referencing Record Types in Formulas" prefers it over the $RecordType
         global everywhere except default-value formulas.

         NOT ON ANY LAYOUT, DELIBERATELY. This field exists to drive Dynamic Actions
         visibility rules (owned by a parallel FlexiPage change), not to be read by a human on
         the record page — a Metadata-API-deployed field is not auto-added to any layout, so
         simply omitting it here is sufficient. It must stay off every Acquisition Broker layout
         too, since it has no meaning for that record type (RecordType.DeveloperName condition
         above is always false there).

         FLS IS LOAD-BEARING. A field deployed through the Metadata API arrives with NO field
         permissions for ANY profile, System Administrator included — the read grant ships in
         the same change (DPEG_IR_Default_Access), and formula fields are read-only by
         construction, so no `editable` grant is meaningful here. -->
    <fullName>Is_Owner_Investor_Onboarding_Queue__c</fullName>
    <label>Is Owner Investor Onboarding Queue?</label>
    <description>Derived, never written directly. True only when the record type is Investor Onboarding AND the current owner is a queue rather than a user — both halves are required, because Acquisition Broker Leads are also queue-owned and would otherwise be misread as belonging to this workflow. Drives Dynamic Actions visibility on the Investor Onboarding Lead record page (queue-owned "assign to me" vs. user-owned next-step actions). Not placed on any layout.</description>
    <inlineHelpText>System field. True when this Lead is Investor Onboarding record type and is still owned by the Investor Onboarding queue (not yet claimed by a user).</inlineHelpText>
    <type>Checkbox</type>
    <formula><![CDATA[AND(
  RecordType.DeveloperName = "Investor_Onboarding",
  LEFT(CASESAFEID(OwnerId), 3) = "00G"
)]]></formula>
    <formulaTreatBlanksAs>BlankAsZero</formulaTreatBlanksAs>
</CustomField>
